# git, because THE APP HALF OF THIS MACHINE IS A GIT CHECKOUT.
#
# FOUND ON THE FIRST REAL CARD 2026-09-13: no substage in stage-elspi listed
# git, none of the upstream stages pulls it in, and the card had to have it
# apt-installed by hand before provisioning could finish. That is a package
# mirror back on the recovery path, which is the one thing docs/design/seam.md's baked
# venv exists to remove.
#
# Two consumers, both load-bearing:
#
#   The DELTA layer. deltas/01-converge.sh drops the reflex monorepo checkout
#   at <app> and runs `uv sync` against it. It now gates on `command -v git`
#   and hard-fails without it (84eabfc), which is loud -- but loud at
#   provisioning time on a machine in a shop is still a trip to a package
#   mirror.
#
#   The IN-APP UPDATER. Setup -> Update runs git fetch/show/checkout against
#   that same checkout. Without git the button refuses, and that is the one
#   path that has to work on a machine with no terminal.
#
# It was installed by stage-elspi/08-venv, the substage for the app's own half
# of the image (the venv is built there from the vendored lock, and the checkout
# git manages is what that venv is eventually synced against). Since 2026-09-26
# it is installed here, in the PACKAGE LAYER (see elspi-base-reuse.sh), with
# elspi's other package-only substages: a layer that is built once and reused
# while its package lists are unchanged, so an emulated build does not reinstall
# them every time. 08-venv still runs after it, and git is on PATH as before.
#
# Named as a package rather than assumed: the whole point of 00-graphics'
# header applies here too -- a dependency that arrives by resolution accident
# is a dependency nobody will notice losing.
git
